#[summary("Benchmarks Game binary-trees(T3-01): 바닥부터 만든 완전 이진 트리의 할당·순회·해제. 깊이 인자 n = 21")]
mod bt {
    enum Tree { Leaf, Node(Box<Tree>, Box<Tree>) }

    spec fn shallow(d: u64) -> bool { d <= 40 }

    #[effects(pure)]
    #[uses(shallow)]
    fn bottom_up(d: u64) -> Box<Tree>
        requires shallow(d),
        decreases d,
    {
        if d == 0 {
            Box::new(Tree::Leaf)
        } else {
            Box::new(Tree::Node(bottom_up(d - 1), bottom_up(d - 1)))
        }
    }

    // The number of nodes (the benchmark's `check`). The count of a tree of depth d is 2^(d+1) - 1;
    // stating it as a contract needs an induction lemma (ADR-0062), so the sum wraps on purpose,
    // as the Rust programs' `+` does in a release build.
    #[effects(pure)]
    fn check(t: &Tree) -> u64
        decreases t,
    {
        match t {
            Tree::Leaf => 1,
            Tree::Node(l, r) => check(&**l).wrapping_add(check(&**r)).wrapping_add(1),
        }
    }

    spec fn label(s: &[u8]) -> bool { s.len() <= 64 }

    #[effects(io)]
    #[uses(label, bytes::room, bytes::grew_by, bytes::kept, bytes::fits, bytes::appended)]
    fn line(a: &[u8], x: u64, b: &[u8], y: u64, c: &[u8], z: u64, three: bool) -> ()
        requires label(a), label(b), label(c),
    {
        let mut out: Vec<u8> = Vec::new();
        bytes::extend(&mut out, a);
        bytes::push_u64(&mut out, x);
        bytes::extend(&mut out, b);
        bytes::push_u64(&mut out, y);
        if three {
            bytes::extend(&mut out, c);
            bytes::push_u64(&mut out, z);
        }
        out.push(b'\n');
        print_bytes(out.as_slice());
    }

    #[effects(io)]
    #[uses(shallow, label)]
    fn main() -> () {
        let n: u64 = 21;
        let min_depth: u64 = 4;
        let max_depth: u64 = if min_depth + 2 > n { min_depth + 2 } else { n };
        let stretch: u64 = max_depth + 1;
        let s: Box<Tree> = bottom_up(stretch);
        line(b"stretch tree of depth ", stretch, b"\t check: ", check(&*s), b"", 0, false);
        let long_lived: Box<Tree> = bottom_up(max_depth);
        let mut d: u64 = min_depth;
        while d <= max_depth
            invariant min_depth <= d, d <= max_depth + 2,
            decreases max_depth + 2 - d,
        {
            let mut iterations: u64 = 1;
            for k in 0..max_depth - d + min_depth {
                iterations = iterations.wrapping_mul(2);
            }
            let mut total: u64 = 0;
            for i in 0..iterations {
                let t: Box<Tree> = bottom_up(d);
                total = total.wrapping_add(check(&*t));
            }
            line(b"", iterations, b"\t trees of depth ", d, b"\t check: ", total, true);
            d = d + 2;
        }
        line(b"long lived tree of depth ", max_depth, b"\t check: ", check(&*long_lived), b"", 0, false);
    }
}
